From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nhat092005 <minhnhat092005@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 08:46:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] drm/bridge: it66121: debounce HPD disconnect glitch

The IT66122 briefly drops the TV HPD signal during HDMI link
re-negotiation approximately 7 seconds into boot. The IRQ handler reads
HPD at the instant of the interrupt and sees "disconnected".
drm_bridge_hpd_notify() propagates this to drm_bridge_connector_hpd_cb(),
which compares old_status (connected) with new_status (disconnected),
detects a change, and fires drm_kms_helper_connector_hotplug_event() ->
drm_fb_helper_restore_fbdev_mode_unlocked() -> CRTC reprogram. The TV
briefly loses sync and re-applies its overscan calibration, visible as a
sudden zoom-in on screen.

Since it66121_irq_threaded_handler() runs in a kernel thread
(IRQF_ONESHOT), sleeping is allowed. When a disconnect event is
detected, sleep 200 ms and re-read the actual HPD state. The IT66122
reconnect completes within ~50-100 ms, so the re-read returns
"connected". drm_bridge_connector_hpd_cb() then sees old_status ==
new_status and returns early, suppressing the re-modeset and zoom.

For a genuine cable-unplug, HPD remains low after 200 ms and the
disconnect is correctly forwarded to the DRM framework.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [product-specific BBB Rev D HDMI fix: debounce HPD disconnect glitch]
Signed-off-by: nhat092005 <minhnhat092005@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/ite-it66121.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/ite-it66121.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/ite-it66121.c
index 1ff39eddf003..a007b5cbb576 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/ite-it66121.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/ite-it66121.c
@@ -975,8 +975,18 @@ static irqreturn_t it66121_irq_threaded_handler(int irq, void *dev_id)
 unlock:
 	mutex_unlock(&ctx->lock);
 
-	if (event)
+	if (event) {
+		if (status == connector_status_disconnected) {
+			/* Debounce transient HPD disconnect from IT66122 HDMI re-negotiation at boot. */
+			msleep(200);
+			mutex_lock(&ctx->lock);
+			status = it66121_is_hpd_detect(ctx) ?
+				connector_status_connected :
+				connector_status_disconnected;
+			mutex_unlock(&ctx->lock);
+		}
 		drm_bridge_hpd_notify(&ctx->bridge, status);
+	}
 
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 }
